(Section 2: Information Article) Tj
ET
0.31 0.27 0.9 RG
1.4173228346456694 w
56.6929133858267775 756.8506299212598378 m
538.5870866141731312 756.8506299212598378 l
S
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 728.5041732283464171 Td
(Introduction to the openEHR Reference Model \(RM\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 688.819133858267719 Td
(openEHR is a technology for storing health data. It helps hospitals and doctors share information) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 668.9766141732283131 Td
(easily. To do this, openEHR uses two main parts. The first part is the Reference Model, or RM. The) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 649.1340944881889072 Td
(second part is the Archetype Model, or AM. In this lesson, we will focus only on the Reference) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 629.291574803149615 Td
(Model \(RM\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 589.6065354330708033 Td
(What is the Reference Model?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 549.9214960629921052 Td
(The Reference Model \(RM\) is the foundation of openEHR. Think of it like the grammar of a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 530.0789763779526993 Td
(language. It provides the rules for how we build sentences. In openEHR, the RM provides the rules) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 510.2364566929133503 Td
(for how we build health records. It defines the 'classes' and 'attributes' that software developers) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 490.3939370078739444 Td
(use. These rules do not change often. They are stable. This stability allows different computer) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 470.5514173228345953 Td
(systems to understand each other.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 430.8663779527558404 Td
(The Structure of the RM) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 391.1813385826770855 Td
(The RM is organized in a hierarchy. This means there are big parts, and inside the big parts, there) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 371.3388188976377364 Td
(are smaller parts. Let us look at the main levels.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 331.6537795275589815 Td
(1. The EHR) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 311.8112598425195756 Td
(At the very top is the EHR class. This represents the entire health record for one patient. It holds all) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 291.9687401574802834 Td
(the documents and folders for that person.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 252.2837007874014716 Td
(2. Composition) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 232.4411811023621794 Td
(Inside the EHR, we have Compositions. A Composition is like a single document. It could be a 'Visit) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 212.5986614173227736 Td
(Note', a 'Discharge Summary', or a 'Lab Report'. Every piece of data in openEHR must belong to a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 192.7561417322833677 Td
(Composition. A Composition always has a 'context'. The context tells us who wrote the document) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 172.9136220472439618 Td
(and when it happened.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 133.2285826771652637 Td
(3. Section) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 113.3860629921258578 Td
(Inside a Composition, we can use Sections. A Section is like a heading in a book. It helps to) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 93.5435433070865656 Td
(organize the information. For example, a document might have a section called 'Family History' or) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 73.7010236220471597 Td
('Current Medicine'. Sections are useful, but they are not mandatory. You can put data directly into a) Tj
ET
endstream
