/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 725.6695275590550409 Td
(The most important part of the RM is the Entry. The Entry is where the real clinical content lives. It) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 705.8270078740157487 Td
(is the statement about the patient. There are four main types of Entries in the RM:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 666.1419685039369369 Td
(- Observation: This is for information collected through seeing, hearing, or measuring. Examples) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 646.2994488188976447 Td
(are blood pressure, temperature, or the patient saying, 'I have a headache.' It is about facts.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 626.4569291338582389 Td
(- Evaluation: This is for the doctor's thinking. It includes the diagnosis or an assessment. It is an) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 606.614409448818833 Td
(opinion based on the observations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 586.7718897637794271 Td
(- Instruction: This is an order. It tells a nurse or another doctor to do something in the future. For) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 566.9293700787401349 Td
(example, 'Give 5mg of aspirin.') Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 547.086850393700729 Td
(- Action: This records what actually happened. If the nurse gives the aspirin, they record an Action.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 527.2443307086614368 Td
(It tracks the progress of an Instruction.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 487.559291338582625 Td
(Data Types) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 447.8742519685038701 Td
(Finally, at the bottom of the structure, we have Data Types. These are the small details. The RM) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 428.0317322834645211 Td
(defines how to write text, numbers, and dates. For example, 'DvText' is for plain words. 'DvQuantity') Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 408.1892125984251152 Td
(is for numbers with units, like '50 kg'.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 368.5041732283464171 Td
(Conclusion) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 328.8191338582676053 Td
(Understanding the RM is the first step to learning openEHR. It gives us the basic blocks: EHR,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 308.9766141732283131 Td
(Composition, Section, and Entry. When we use these blocks correctly, we create safe and clear) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 289.1340944881889072 Td
(health records.) Tj
ET
