/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 677.480551181102328 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 677.480551181102328 Td
(That is great. Today, we will talk about the Reference Model. We often call it the RM. Have) Tj
T* (you heard of the RM before?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 637.7955118110235162 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 637.7955118110235162 Td
(I have heard the name, but I do not know what it means. Is it a computer program?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 612.2837007874015853 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 612.2837007874015853 Td
(Not exactly. It is not a program you run. It is a set of rules. It is a model for information.) Tj
T* (Think of it like a blueprint for a house.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 572.5986614173227736 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 572.5986614173227736 Td
(A blueprint. Okay. So it tells us how to build the health record?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 547.086850393700729 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 547.086850393700729 Td
(Yes, exactly. It defines the structure. In openEHR, we have two levels. One is the RM, and) Tj
T* (the other is the Archetypes. Today, we only look at the RM.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 507.4018110236219741 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 507.4018110236219741 Td
(Okay. Only the RM. What is the most important thing in the RM?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 481.8899999999999295 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 481.8899999999999295 Td
(The RM has many classes. A class is a group of data. The biggest class is the EHR. EHR) Tj
T* (stands for Electronic Health Record.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 442.2049606299212314 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 442.2049606299212314 Td
(I see. So the EHR class is the whole file for the patient?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 416.69314960629913 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 416.69314960629913 Td
(Yes. Every patient has one EHR. Inside the EHR, we have documents. In the RM, we call) Tj
T* (a document a 'Composition'.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 377.0081102362204319 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 377.0081102362204319 Td
(Composition. That is a new word for me. Can you give me an example of a Composition?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 351.4962992125983874 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 351.4962992125983874 Td
(Sure. When you go to the doctor, the doctor writes notes. That note is a Composition. If) Tj
T* (you get a blood test, the result paper is a Composition.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 311.8112598425195756 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 311.8112598425195756 Td
(I understand. A Composition is one event or one report. What is inside the Composition?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 286.2994488188975311 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 286.2994488188975311 Td
(Good question. A Composition contains 'Content'. We can organize this content using) Tj
T* ('Sections'.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 246.614409448818833 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 246.614409448818833 Td
(Sections? Like chapters in a book?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 221.1025984251967884 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 221.1025984251967884 Td
(Yes, exactly like chapters. You might have a Section for 'Allergies' and a Section for) Tj
T* ('Medications'. But Sections are optional. You do not always need them.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 181.4175590551179766 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 181.4175590551179766 Td
(Okay. If I do not use a Section, what do I use? What holds the actual data?) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 155.9057480314959321 Td
(Jane:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 155.9057480314959321 Td
(The actual clinical data lives in the 'Entry' classes. The Entry is the most important part of) Tj
T* (the RM for clinical details.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.31 0.275 0.898 rg
56.6929133858267775 116.220708661417234 Td
(Joe:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
127.5590551181102512 116.220708661417234 Td
(Entry. Okay. Are there different types of Entries?) Tj
ET
